// A simulation on its own: the engine and its viewer, standing no robot.
// This is the command for a machine whose job is the simulation and
// nothing else.
//
//   peppy stack launch simulation                             # Waldo and its viewer
//   peppy stack launch simulation --with isaac_sim
//   peppy stack launch simulation --with web_scene_commander  # the scene panel with it
//
// The simulation runs on the machine the launch is sent to: this one, or
// the one `--core-node` names. Waldo serves its viewer and the hand teleop
// panel on viewer_port (8080) and Isaac Sim its WebRTC frontend on 8210.
// The scene panel, on 8766, is the axis each of them declares, so it takes
// the launch word above: spawn, move and remove objects, and list what
// stands in the scene.
//
// This file declares no robot axis, so nothing joins it. A robot stands in
// a simulation the same launch names, which is what
// openarm/openarm_simulation.json5, so101/so101_simulation.json5 and
// mcp/simulation_mcp.json5 do.
//
// MuJoCo is no option here: it answers no scene call, so nothing in this
// launch could command it. It runs a robot's own simulation in the
// launchers above.
{
  peppy_schema: "launcher/v1",

  components: [
    {
      name: "simulation",
      cardinality: "one",
      options: {
        isaac_sim: "fragments/isaac_sim.json5",
        waldo: "fragments/waldo.json5",
      },
    },
  ],

  deployments: [
    { simulation: "waldo" },
  ],
}
